duplicates: 786 items in 381 groups (10.2s)
</code></pre>
<p>One nice thing about this is now I can search all of my Denote notes from my phone.</p>
<p>Everything is plain files and it uses boring, durable tools, so the archive should outlive whichever apps made the content that week. Even an AI layer, if I add one, sits on top of the search instead of being built into it. The database is disposable because it only takes 10 seconds to reindex everything.</p>
<p>Maybe now I'll be OK with all of my app churn.</p>
